"name\":\"\",\"type\":\"address\"},{\"internalType\":\"bytes32\",\"name\":\"\",\"type\":\"bytes32\"}],\"name\":\"verdictTrue\",\"outputs\":[{\"internalType\":\"bool\",\"name\":\"\",\"type\":\"bool\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\",\"type\":\"function\"}],\"devdoc\":{\"details\":\"NOT trustless and NOT an oracle. This chain cannot read GenLayer. The carrier is trusted to post      only a finalized TRUE verdict; this contract checks only that the carrier the delegator signed      for did post TRUE for exactly this case. What the carrier cannot do: post for another carrier,      change the amount, the recipient or any other caveat, or un-post. Deny is the default: there is      no way to post FALSE, so a case that never gets a TRUE from its carrier is never payable.      Terms: abi.encode(bytes32 caseKey, address carrier), exactly 64 bytes.      caseKey = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\\\"internet-court-mandate-verdict\\\", genlayerChainId, caseContract)),      the same value the off-chain code uses as the delegation salt.      Standalone on purpose (no imports): the four hooks match ICaveatEnforcer of Delegation Framework      v1.3.0, where ModeCode is a bytes32 user-defined value type, so the selectors are identical.\",\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{},\"title\":\"VerdictGateEnforcer\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"beforeHook(bytes,bytes,bytes32,bytes,bytes32,address,address)\":{\"notice\":\"The gate. Called by the DelegationManager before the delegated execution runs.\"},\"caseKey(uint256,address)\":{\"notice\":\"The case key (delegation salt) for a GenLayer MandateVerdict contract.\"},\"getTermsInfo(bytes)\":{\"notice\":\"Decode caveat terms.\"},\"postVerdictTrue(uint256,address)\":{\"notice\":\"Record, as msg.sender, that this GenLayer case resolved TRUE. Only delegations whose         terms name msg.sender as the carrier are affected.\"},\"verdictTrue(address,bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"carrier => caseKey => TRUE recorded. Write-once; never cleared.\"}},\"notice\":\"Caveat enforcer for MetaMask's Delegation Framework (ERC-7710). A delegation that carries         this caveat can be redeemed only after the carrier named in its terms has recorded, on this         chain, that the GenLayer case named in its terms resolved TRUE.\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"src/VerdictGateEnforcer.sol\":\"VerdictGateEnforcer\"},\"evmVersion\":\"shanghai\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":200},\"remappings\":[]},\"sources\":{\"src/VerdictGateEnforcer.sol\":{\"keccak256\":\"0xfb2b6f0dd0441b77d27e67e2c3a1dee8ac7103ee302f1ee628edf0cca79439b8\",\"license\":\"MIT\",\"urls\":[\"bzz-raw://e696bc5853e7f32d7f47dc98ae837fddd0fe114797f0b8380e063fdf282f4fa7\",\"dweb:/ipfs/QmPsEf6bNy7hJAiJXUuAKCQhLwtAV6PhbNu3C7kEU7ZJYD\"]}},\"version\":1}"
